  faqs: [
    { question: "How do I find an IB tutor in Etawah?", answer: "Write to us with your child's programme, subject, level and the session they're sitting, and a shortlist follows built entirely on who has actually taught that course. Since Etawah has no IB school of its own, geography plays no part in the shortlist at all, only whether a tutor's background genuinely matches. A free trial lesson happens before anything is decided, and a different tutor is easy to arrange if the first isn't right." },
    { question: "Do you offer IGCSE tutors in Etawah for Cambridge or Edexcel?", answer: "Yes, for both boards, and always as online tuition since neither runs at any school inside the district. A request gets matched down to the code and tier, say Mathematics 0580 Extended or Chemistry 0620, and lessons work from that board's actual past papers rather than generic revision material." },
    { question: "Do your tutors visit homes in Etawah?", answer: "No, they do not. House visits are something IB Gram offers only in Gurugram and pockets of Delhi NCR; an Etawah lesson happens live over video, one to one, with both sides sharing a screen. It's genuine online tuition delivered to your home, just never a tutor physically stepping into it." },
    { question: "What does an IB or IGCSE tutor in Etawah cost?", answer: "Cost depends on the programme, subject, level, session length and how recently a tutor has taught that specific syllabus, and it's settled for your particular match before the trial lesson, not adjusted later. Diploma HL work generally costs more than IGCSE Core support. Nothing gets added for travel since every lesson is online, and there's no long-term contract locking a family in." },
    { question: "Are there any IB or IGCSE schools in Etawah?", answer: "None. Every school inside Etawah district, Kendriya Vidyalaya and Jawahar Navodaya Vidyalaya in Civil Lines included, runs UP Board or CBSE rather than an international curriculum. The closest confirmed Cambridge IGCSE campuses are in Kanpur and Agra, both around 130 to 140 kilometres away by road." },
    { question: "My child studied IB or IGCSE elsewhere before we moved to Etawah. Can a tutor continue it?", answer: "Yes, and this is one of the requests we hear most from Etawah, since families often arrive here mid-course through a government, paramilitary or business posting. A tutor picks up exactly where the previous school left off, on the same subject, level and syllabus, rather than starting the course over from the beginning." },
    { question: "Is there a free trial lesson before I commit?", answer: "There is, on every single match. Your child spends the trial working through a genuine topic from their own syllabus, with nothing charged and nothing owed afterward. A short plan for the first month follows from the tutor, and you're free to proceed, ask for adjustments, or simply try someone else instead." },
    { question: "Can a tutor help with IB Internal Assessments for a child in Etawah?", answer: "Yes, in an advisory role only, never by writing content. That covers narrowing down a workable research question, unpacking what each criterion is really asking for, thinking through data collection, and reading drafts honestly. Anything closer to writing or rewriting the assessment itself breaches IB integrity rules, so that request gets turned down." },
    { question: "Which IB Diploma subjects can you help with for an Etawah family?", answer: "Coverage spans essentially every major Diploma subject group a boarding or relocated Etawah student might need: both Maths routes at HL and SL, Physics, Chemistry, Biology, Economics, Business Management, English A, Computer Science, plus Theory of Knowledge support and Extended Essay guidance." },
    { question: "Do you tutor IB MYP and PYP students connected to Etawah, not only the Diploma?", answer: "Yes, right across the continuum. A family in Etawah with a child enrolled at an IB school elsewhere, or shifting between curricula, can get MYP support built around criterion-based marking and the Personal Project, or PYP support built around reading, number confidence and Exhibition research." },
    { question: "Is online tutoring as effective as in-person tuition for IB or IGCSE students in Etawah?", answer: "It holds up well, especially given that Etawah has no local specialist for any IB or Cambridge subject to begin with. A shared screen, past papers marked live and worked-through solutions replicate most of what sitting beside a tutor would offer, while opening up specialists from anywhere in India instead of nobody nearby." },
    { question: "How are IB Gram tutors verified for Etawah students?", answer: "Each tutor's qualifications, recent teaching history on the exact subject and level, and grasp of the relevant assessment criteria all get checked before any introduction happens. With no local school to draw comparisons from, we specifically look for someone who has taught the current syllabus recently rather than a generalist. The trial lesson then lets a family judge fit for themselves." },
    { question: "When should my child in Etawah start IB or IGCSE tutoring?", answer: "Starting right at the beginning, Class 11 for the Diploma or Grade 9 for IGCSE, gives the most room to fix gaps before internal deadlines, IA work and predicted grades all converge later. Starting in the final year still helps meaningfully, with sessions focused tightly on the highest-value topics and timed past papers." },
    { question: "My child is moving from UP Board or CBSE to IGCSE. Can a tutor help with the switch?", answer: "Yes, and it's a fairly regular request, usually tied to a planned move to a Cambridge school in Kanpur or Agra. The gap is rarely the content itself; it's the question style. Words like explain, evaluate and justify need direct, deliberate teaching, ideally a term ahead of the actual switch rather than after it." },
    { question: "Can sessions happen on weekends or after school hours in Etawah?", answer: "Yes, weekday evenings and weekend mornings are what most Etawah families book. Scheduling factors in the district's harsh summer heat, when an earlier evening slot usually works better, and the disruption winter fog or Saifai Mahotsav crowds can bring some years. A second weekly session ahead of mocks is simple to add." },
    { question: "What happens if we are not happy with the tutor in Etawah?", answer: "Tell us, and a different tutor gets found. Families are checked in with every few weeks specifically so a wrong fit doesn't drag on, and there's no expectation that a child simply adjusts to someone who isn't working out. No contract means pausing or stopping never comes with a penalty attached." },
    { question: "Is IB Gram affiliated with any school near Etawah, or with the IB, Cambridge or Edexcel?", answer: "No, on every count. IB Gram operates independently, with no affiliation, endorsement or representation tied to any school named on this page, nor to the International Baccalaureate Organization, Cambridge Assessment International Education or Pearson Edexcel. Named schools simply describe where nearby families sometimes look, and tutors follow each board's own published syllabus and calendar." },
  ],

